From: Thingino <dev@thingino.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hal: throttle the T31 idle-poll log line by time

0001 polls non-blocking on T31, so an idle video channel reaches the miss
path every couple of milliseconds instead of once per 500 ms timeout. The
line was throttled to one per 20 misses, which on that cadence still
prints ~5 lines a second: the syslog ring is 644 lines, so it rotated in
under two minutes and took the boot diagnostics with it - the sensor
attach and clock bring-up lines were gone by the time anyone looked.

Throttle by time (one line per 5 s) and leave dbg_pollfail alone: it is
the watchdog's miss counter, not a log counter. The jpeg_thread line is
not touched - with a dedicated JPEG channel its misses are rare, and on
the piggyback configuration it is idle rather than spinning.

Measured on cinnado_d1_t31l_sc2336_atbm6031 (7.2.11, OpenIMP): 598 lines
in 107 s before, ring intact after.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>

--- a/src/hal/hal_ingenic.c
+++ b/src/hal/hal_ingenic.c
@@ -3400,9 +3400,21 @@
         if (pr!=0 || gs_fail){
             if (receiving){
                 if (++dbg_pollfail == 1) miss_t0 = ms_now_us();
-                if (!gs_fail && (dbg_pollfail % 20)==1)
-                    LOGW(MOD,"chn%d: PollingStream idle (rc=%d, miss#%d) - encoder emits no frames",
-                         vc->chn, pr, dbg_pollfail);
+                /* The T31 build polls non-blocking (see the workaround
+                 * above), so an idle channel reaches this miss path every
+                 * couple of milliseconds: a line per 20 misses still printed
+                 * ~5 lines a second and rotated the syslog ring in under two
+                 * minutes, taking the boot diagnostics with it. Throttle the
+                 * line by time and leave dbg_pollfail to the watchdog. */
+                if (!gs_fail){
+                    static int64_t poll_log_us;
+                    int64_t log_now = ms_now_us();
+                    if (log_now - poll_log_us >= 5000000){
+                        poll_log_us = log_now;
+                        LOGW(MOD,"chn%d: PollingStream idle (rc=%d, miss#%d) - encoder emits no frames",
+                             vc->chn, pr, dbg_pollfail);
+                    }
+                }
                 if (dbg_pollfail >= MS_VIDEO_WATCHDOG_ITERS &&
                     ms_now_us() - miss_t0 >= MS_WATCHDOG_MIN_US){
                     dbg_recover_fails++;
